<title>ITALY: Italian train fares to rise 2.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Italian train fares to rise 2.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian economic policy officials said on Thursday they had given the green light to a 2.5 percent rise in the price of train tickets.</p>
<p>An official of the Interminsterial Committee for Economic Policy (CIPE) said the rise would now pass to Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi to be signed.</p>
<p>The official said the price increases would have a 0.011 percent impact on the consumer price index and would probably take effect on March 1.</p>
<p>Italy's railways are run by a state-owned company, Ferrovie dello Stato.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
